In response to Ralph (rwirthli@nyx.cs.du.edu):

  I think a major problem with doing Nethack as a Doomgame is 
that
Doom is by nature a realtime game, and Nethack is not. I would
be most peeved to be killed by a marauding monster while I was
deciding what weapon or spell to use. Making Nethack realtime
would reduce it to a shoot-em-up, with little time to decide
between one option and another.
  Personally, I like to be able to go through my inventory when
I'm surrounded and pick the best wand or spell or weapon. Doom
is good, but notice how you've got only a small choice of 
weapons?
  Also, with Nethack's overhead view, you can see the 
approaching
hoardes - all of them, not just the ones in front of you.
Implementing something like telepathy would be a problem in a
Doomgame. And if you're going to stop the game in order to 
allow 
choices to be made, why bother making it realtime in the first 
place?
  Anyway, I guess it comes back to my original point - if you 
convert
Nethack to 3D what you get when you're finished isn't Nethack.

Still my opinions,  Joel  :)
